  "stpkp.w.mu.txt": "Multiply the thief's utilities by <i>μ</i>: small <i>μ</i> is a thief who picks almost at random, large <i>μ</i> one who almost always takes the best option. Theorem 2 applied to <i>μα</i> and <i>μβ</i> gives the location weights e<sup><i>α<sub>i</sub></i>/(1/<i>μ</i> + Σ<sub><i>L</i></sub><i>β</i>)</sup>, with Σ<sub><i>L</i></sub><i>β</i> = {b} here: they run from the equal split towards the fair weights of Theorem 3, the answer to a deterministic thief (Theorem 4). The constant 1 of Theorem 2 is the size of the thief's randomness (this guide's reading).",
